WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
[Upbeat instrumental music]
Jackalope. Your next idea. Already in motion.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Make it yours.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Choose light or dark, explore colors, and keep your workspace theme.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A place to start.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Choose a project, enable its agents, and set its appearance.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Jackalope prepares the workspace and opens your first task.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Describe it. Dispatch it.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Write the outcome you want. Review the task options and start work.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Beyond the editor. Browser and computer tools.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
A sample browser workflow: search for an event and reserve a place.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Return to Jackalope to inspect check results and screenshot evidence.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Your agents. All your accounts.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Codex, Claude Code, Grok, and OpenCode. Keep work and personal sign-ins together.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
See the connections.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Explore the codebase map. Open a directory and inspect a file’s dependencies.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
More room to build. jackalope.dev
Sample-data walkthrough; no native agent task launched.
